%S A402566 1,1,1,3,1,1,3,5,1,2,3,1,5,7,1,1,2,3,3,2,5,1,7,1,0,1,3,2,6,3,3,5,1,6,
%T A402566 2,7,1,0,1,4,1,5,2,8,3,1,4,5,5,2,6,3,7,1,8,2,0,1,8,1,8,2,1,0,3,2,4,7,
%U A402566 5,3,6,5,7,4,8,4,0,2,1,1,1,1,2,1,2,3,5
%N A402566 Digits of the decimal self-stirring word: start with 1, cycle through labels 0,...,9, skip zero counts, otherwise append the current count followed by its label, updating all counts immediately.
%H A402566 Lei Zhou (SWUST), <a href="/A402566/b402566.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A402566 Lei Zhou, <a href="https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202610.1633/v2">Self-Stirring Sequences: Exact Dynamics and Statistical Rigidity</a>, Preprints.org, version 2, November 19, 2026.
%F A402566 For any fixed decimal word w of length k, the number of its overlapping occurrences among a(1),...,a(N), divided by N, is 10^(-k) + O(log(log(N))/log(N)). Thus 0.a(1)a(2)... is normal to base 10. See Zhou, Theorem 2.6.
%e A402566 The words at the first round boundaries are 1, 111, 1113113, 1113113512315. In round 2, the visit to label 1 appends 31; label 3 then has count 1 and appends 13 during the same round.
%o A402566 (Python)
%o A402566 def terms():
%o A402566     c = [0]*10
%o A402566     c[1] = 1
%o A402566     yield 1
%o A402566     while True:
%o A402566         for d in range(10):
%o A402566             q = c[d]
%o A402566             if q:
%o A402566                 block = list(map(int, str(q))) + [d]
%o A402566                 for x in block:
%o A402566                     c[x] += 1
%o A402566                 yield from block
%Y A402566 Cf. A402567 (positive counts), A402568 (lengths after complete rounds).
%K A402566 nonn,base,easy,new
%O A402566 1,4
%A A402566 _Lei Zhou (SWUST)_, Nov 21 2026
